## First function of the updateSpeakerIdentities, updateCallSummaryText and
## updateCallAgenda pipelines: read the meeting's Owner and SharedWith, so the
## write that follows can hold a signed-in caller to the access rule getCall
## applies -- Admin, the meeting's owner, or an entry of its SharedWith -- in
## every shape SharedWith is stored in. A DynamoDB condition alone cannot split a
## String into entries, so the entries are read here and the write's condition
## re-checks what was found; see authorizeCallWrite.response.vtl.
##
## The read runs for every caller, Admins and backend roles included, although
## only a signed-in non-Admin caller's condition uses what it records: one
## pipeline for every caller keeps the stash the write reads always present.
{
  "version" : "2018-05-29",
  "operation" : "GetItem",
  "key": {
    "PK": $util.dynamodb.toDynamoDBJson("c#${ctx.args.input.CallId}"),
    "SK": $util.dynamodb.toDynamoDBJson("c#${ctx.args.input.CallId}")
  },
  "consistentRead": true
}
